     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I don&#39;t understand the output of the modificationIndices function. Here is the SEM model:</div><div> </div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">modelR </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> <br><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&#39; <br> # Mastery measures <br><br> factor1 =~ Q19.1 + Q19.2 + Q19.3 + Q19.4 + Q19.5 <br> factor2 =~ Q19.6 + Q19.7 <br><br> # Social support measures <br><br> factor3 =~ Q35.1 + Q35.3 + Q35.4 + Q35.6 + Q35.8 + Q35.10 <br> factor4 =~ Q35.2 + Q35.5 + Q35.7 + Q35.9 <br><br><br> # Regressions on observed, dependent variables. <br><br> Var5 ~ factor1 + factor2 + factor3 + factor4 + Var7 + Var1 + Var2 + Var3 +  Var8 <br><br> Var6 ~ factor1 + factor2 + factor3 + factor4 + Var7 + Var1 + Var2 + Var3 +  Var8 <br><br> Var4 ~ factor1 + factor2 + factor3 + factor4 + Var7 + Var1 + Var2 + Var3 +  Var8 <br><br> &#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> <br> fit</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">R </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> sem</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">modelR</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> data</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mData</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> <br><br><br><br></span></div></code></div><font size=\"2\"><p><br></p><div>When I look at the modification indices, I see MI&#39;s for parameters that I thought were already free. Here is a sample of the output.</div><div> </div><font size=\"2\"><p>  </p><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div